// ==========================================================================
// FULL CONNECTOME C. elegans - hermaphrodite
// 302 neurons (282 somatic + 20 pharyngeal) + 148 targets
// (95 body muscles, 22 pharyngeal muscles, 31 other targets).
// Data: Cook et al. 2019 / OpenWorm herm_full_edgelist.csv.
//
// CONVENTIONS
// - chemical weight synapse = synapse count / 40: the operating point is chosen so that
// the bilateral sensory pathway FLP->AVA (~114 total, ~57 per cell)
// has a total weight of ~1.4 — comparable to 1.0 of the tested nose-touch
// circuit (there, the L+R pools were merged and the normalization was /114)
// - gap junction conductance = contact count / 100
// - sign: -1 for GABAergic (DD01-06, VD01-13, RMED/L/R/V, AVL, DVB, RIS)
// - release threshold rel = 1.0, slope 5, tau=0.1 s, bias=-0.1, noise 0.1
// - gap: g*(p-v) = glin(Σ g_j p_j) - G*v, G = Σ g_j — cell literal
// - dendritic aggregators d_*_N (chemistry) and g_* (gap) are memoized per tick
// - 48 autosynapses from the data (M4->M4 x15, RIML->RIML x11, ...) are retained
//
// RUN
// - with host: publish 'touch' (0..1) — nose touch; read 'AVAL'...'AVER'
// - without host: autonomous random_touch (strength U[0,1], pause 5-10 sec) +
// monitors print command neurons 4 times per second
//
// CHECKED WITH MIRROR SIMULATION (Python, same equations, 120 sec):
// - stable: max|v| = 3.1, no divergence
// - rest: 0% active neurons, AVA=-0.07, AVB=-0.08
// - nose touch: dose-response as in nose-touch: force <0.3 — no response,
// 0.5-0.9 — reversal (AVA up to 1.8, AVB suppressed to 0.2), 8/14 touches —
// reversal, return to rest in ~2 s
// =========================================================================

// -------- time and incentive --------
'touch' host_touch;
simtime clock(1.);
random_touch rnd_touch();
first_defined touch(host_touch, rnd_touch);

// -------- NEW SENSORS (touch stimulus input): ASH, FLP, OLQ, IL1: 14 in total --------
